{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792506757,"nonce":"foOqMM8CWPUgHCQNATKg1bOE7SM=","message":"Implemented in 18e160fd83f7c31a5f1277cf888bf68508018ef9.\n\nThe shared API now accepts TypedDeclaration::Initializer(TypedInitializer { body, annotations, module: None }). A frontend supplies a top-level block rather than an entry function. Empty and function-only files need neither declaration. Shared preparation moves blocks into private, module-qualified internal functions before type checking and pattern rewriting; HIR carries their ordered ids in HirModule.initializers. Existing functions and explicit host entry points retain their behavior.\n\nInitializers are implicit reachability roots for closed scripts and additional host roots for entry-driven codegen. Open libraries retain their ordinary callable functions. Source imports retain dependency and declaration order; prelowered imports supply signature references in the same ordering stream, keeping their bodies encoded until needed. The function-less HIR image and snapshot relocation retain initializer ids. Snapshot interfaces strip initializer bodies along with other executable bodies. Already installed snapshot initializers are skipped during joins.\n\nTieredRuntime and ZyntaxRuntime run initialization after installing code, symbols and globals. Successful initializer ids are recorded per runtime, so subsequent imports do not repeat their effects. Failure stops loading and is cached on the runtime, preventing calls from proceeding through failed initialization. Tiered execution still starts in the interpreter; native promotion does not repeat initialization. Per-function optimization scratch modules do not copy initialization lists. Generated marker names are interned once and new compilation maps use Fx hashing.\n\nTypeScript now emits a block only when there are top-level statements. zynode loads that program without declaring or calling ts$main; a source function named main is an ordinary TypeScript function. Strict floating-point annotations, static release analysis, typed array GEPs, aliases and generic specializations remain covered by the existing suites. The snapshot tests no longer need to remove an empty library entry manually.\n\nValidation:\n- 51 TypeScript tests pass with default features and with LLVM/allocation-audit enabled, including pinned acceptance/output checks for all 214 fixtures.\n- The full conformance harness passes 642/642 runs: 214 fixtures across interpreter, Cranelift and LLVM profiles. No KNOWN_FAILURES entries were added.\n- Five new fixtures were checked against TypeScript 6.0.2/Node: empty file, declaration-only library, ordinary source main, statement order and a long top-level loop. All 15 live profile comparisons pass.\n- Six shared initializer regressions pass with default and LLVM features: explicit entries and DCE roots, source dependency sharing/order, mixed source/snapshot ordering, selective snapshot imports/relocation/repeated loads/joins, cached initialization failure, and open classic-runtime function calls after initialization.\n- Shared bytecode (14), monomorphization (11), prelowered linking (6), snapshot (13), compiled artifact (2), import-chain (4), reachability (1) and borrowed-image (1) regressions pass. The unused-generic allocation profile passes explicitly.\n- Python and Lua cargo check pass against the changed shared APIs. Formatting and clippy with LLVM/allocation-audit and -D warnings pass.\n\nFormat changes: bytecode major 9, compiled-import schema 4, snapshot schema 10. Previous artifacts require rebuilding. The existing incompatible-HIR fallback issue 5e24efcb4fb48c15ac0ad0a57dee42ab4308d831fc0a4e8ea988709a4e5bf18f remains tracked independently.\n\nFull TypeScript import/export syntax, resolution and public symbol scoping remain in 0c26889a7cd2c4060eb94ef93fd808c2857089dbf714735ca52b5d071bdb1564. This change removes the requirement for a source-level main and the empty-entry collision; it does not close that broader module issue.","files":null}]}